From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:41:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: automatic columns widen cells on expanded
 windows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Automatic columns (preference 0) used a 128 dp cell in the book grids and a
two-step panorama tier (112 dp under 600 dp, 140 dp from there up). An unfolded
landscape window, 939 dp, then fit 7 columns in browse and 6 in panorama.

The minimum is now one width tier for browse and the library, panorama and
book grids. It follows the window-size breakpoints: 112 dp under 600 dp,
140 dp under 840 dp, and 176 dp from 840 dp up. The lane count is
(available + 4) / (min + 4), with available = window width - 16 dp.
459 dp is 3, 664 dp is 4, and 939 dp is 5. A fixed count from 1 to 10 is
unchanged.

Unknown panorama shelves use that minimum directly. Tall and wide shelves
still size from the cover shape, and the tier minimum is a floor on the
lane width, so a tall shelf on a 939 dp window stays at 5.

与 anikku-harmony 同病（同一段代码 / 同一套网格），Anikku 侧待移植。
